From 77a708d953a7667155729983909a382d309acb42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MentorLink Admin Agent <admin-agent@mentorlink.local>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 04:46:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix "Network connection error" causes, missing card
 buttons, and list pagination

Root causes found for the admin Mini App failing on every click:

- CORS only allowed GET/POST/OPTIONS, but the admin app uses PATCH (verification
  checklist, resolving incidents) and DELETE (removing admins). Browsers reject those
  at the preflight, which surfaces as a generic network error. Tests could not see
  this because they call the API directly. Now allows PUT/PATCH/DELETE.
- Unhandled server errors were returned by Starlette's outermost handler with no CORS
  headers, so a real 500 (e.g. migrations not applied) also looked like a network
  error. Added a global handler returning JSON + CORS headers + a reference id that
  matches the server log.
- Production does not create tables, and /health only ran SELECT 1, so a database
  behind the deployed migrations reported "healthy". /health now reports
  schema_state (current/behind/untracked) and the app logs an ERROR at startup when
  behind.
- Added CORS_EXTRA_ORIGINS so a frontend on a different domain can be allowed.

"Review in App" buttons silently missing:
- get_admin_review_url required MINI_APP_URL to be a t.me link and returned None
  without any log otherwise. It now falls back to https://t.me/<bot>/<short name>
  (ADMIN_MINI_APP_SHORT_NAME) and logs a one-time warning when it cannot build a link.

Security:
- CRON_SECRET no longer has a hardcoded default (the old value was public in this
  repo). Comparison is now constant-time.

Assignment notifications:
- Assigning already DMs parent and tutor; it was untested and swallowed failures
  silently. Added tests (both DMs sent; a failed DM does not break the assignment)
  and warning logs instead of bare except/pass.

Pagination/search:
- TutorList: server-side search by name/phone (debounced) + pager (was capped at 50
  with no way to see more). New `search` param on GET /admin/tutors.
- Audit log and Incidents: pagers added. OpsQueue no longer hides load failures behind
  an empty "nothing found" state.

Frontend api client:
- Network failures are recognised by error type instead of Chrome's exact wording
  ("Load failed" on iOS Telegram and Firefox's message previously leaked through),
  the message now names the API host and the app's origin, and idempotent GETs retry
  once (writes are never auto-retried).

Docs: .env.example and RUNBOOK corrected (MINI_APP_URL is the t.me link), release
checklist with alembic upgrade head, and a network-error troubleshooting guide.

Tests: 88 -> 107. New tests fail against the old behaviour (verified).
