From 26873135429c56d69e50a1561fbf65b15ad9f0ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MentorLink Admin Agent <admin-agent@mentorlink.local>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:38:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Stop guessing the Mini App short name; diagnose "Review
 in App" opening the bot

"Review in App" opened the bot chat instead of the app. The link is built from
MINI_APP_URL, and Telegram only opens an app when https://t.me/<bot>/<short_name>
matches an app registered with /newapp on that bot; otherwise it silently opens the
bot chat. DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE registered the admin app as ".../admin" but told operators
to set MINI_APP_URL to the main app link ".../app", so the two never matched.

- ADMIN_MINI_APP_SHORT_NAME no longer defaults to "admin". A guessed name that is not
  registered produces exactly this symptom, so it is now explicit opt-in.
- New startup self-check logs the exact link cards will use, warns when MINI_APP_URL
  has no short name, and tells the operator what to verify in BotFather /myapps.
- DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE: MINI_APP_URL is the ADMIN app link; ENVIRONMENT default is
  "development" in code (was documented as "production"), which makes the app run
  create_all and conflict with Alembic; added troubleshooting for both.
- Tests reproduce the reported mix-up (registered "admin" vs configured "app").
