 #### Q4: Alembic migration fails during deployment?
 - **Cause:** Database URL is using `postgresql://` instead of `postgresql+asyncpg://` or database user lacks table creation privileges.
 - **Solution:** Ensure `DATABASE_URL` uses the async driver: `postgresql+asyncpg://<user>:<pass>@<host>/<db>`. Run `alembic upgrade head`.
+- **If the error is `relation ... already exists` / `column ... already exists`:** the tables were created outside Alembic, almost always by the app's own `create_all`, which runs whenever `ENVIRONMENT` is not `production`. Set `ENVIRONMENT=production`. For a database that already has the tables, do not drop columns or edit migrations: back it up, confirm the schema matches the models, then run `alembic stamp head` once.
 
+#### Q5: "Review in App" opens the bot chat instead of the Mini App?
+- **Cause:** Telegram only opens the app when `https://t.me/<bot>/<short_name>` matches an app registered with `/newapp` on that same bot. Otherwise it silently opens the bot chat.
+- **Solution:** In @BotFather send `/myapps`, choose the bot and read the admin app's short name. Set `MINI_APP_URL=https://t.me/<bot>/<that short name>` (the startup log prints the resulting link), and make sure the app's Web App URL ends in `/admin.html`. Redeploy, then use a *new* card: old cards keep the old link.
